# OpenShift Shell: Unsandboxed

Observed failure (2026-09-30): Cursor **Agent Shell** defaults to a sandbox where
`oc whoami` fails with `Forbidden` / “Not logged into OpenShift” even though
`~/.kube/config` has a valid interactive login. With
`required_permissions: ["all"]`, the same command succeeds.

## Prefer MCP for cluster API

For pods, logs, events, Helm, Routes, operators → use **`user-kubernetes`** MCP
(`openshift-mcp` skill). Do **not** use sandboxed `oc` for those.

## Shell must request `all` when

Any of the following run in the **Shell** tool (not MCP):

| Pattern | Examples |
|---|---|
| OpenShift CLI | `oc …`, `kubectl …` |
| OpenShell CLI | `openshell …` |
| Presenter / observability | `./scripts/demo-presenter-serve.sh`, `demo-observability-proxy.py` |
| Deploy / verify / demo scripts | `make -C deploy …`, `./scripts/launch-openclaw.sh`, `./scripts/verify.sh`, `./scripts/demo-*.sh`, `./scripts/cluster-lifecycle.sh` |

Invoke Shell with:

```text
required_permissions: ["all"]
```

## If `oc whoami` fails

1. Retry the **same** command with `required_permissions: ["all"]` (do not tell the user to re-login yet).
2. Only if unsandboxed `oc whoami` still fails → ask the user to run `oc login` in their interactive terminal.
3. Never commit kubeconfig, tokens, or paste login tokens into the repo or chat.

## Do not

- Assume “Not logged in” from a sandboxed Shell means the workstation session is dead
- Start `demo-presenter-serve.sh` without `["all"]` (preflight will false-fail)
- Store cluster credentials in project files to “fix” agent auth
